nodes.prompt:
Plan exactly 3 distinct YouTube thumbnail concepts for this video. Each must read instantly at small size: one clear focal subject, high contrast, bold saturated colors, a simple uncluttered background, and big headline text of at most 4 words (not the full title). Vary the angle across the three (e.g. emotion/reaction, before-vs-after or comparison, curiosity/mystery object).

If a reference image URL is given, every concept must feature that face or product as the main subject; describe how it is posed, framed and lit, but do not invent a different person. Do not imitate real creators, logos or trademarks, and avoid misleading or shocking imagery.

For each concept output:
- Name (2-3 words)
- Overlay text (max 4 words, uppercase)
- Image prompt (max 80 words, landscape 16:9): subject, expression, composition with space for the text, lighting, color palette, style. Put the overlay text in the prompt in double quotes so the model renders it.
- Why it works (one line)

Video title: {{inputs.title}}
Reference image URL: {{inputs.image_url}}
Channel style / audience: {{inputs.notes}}
